# kat/lkmm-genmc.kat is not extensible. The write e2 is in a hole before the
# read e3 of its location, which reads e5 from T1: coherence puts e2 mo-before
# e5, its only place in mo, and e2 -moe-> e5 closes the pb cycle e2 -prop-> e5
# -strong-fence-> e7, e7 -prop-> e0 -strong-fence-> e2 (prop: e2 -moe-> e5,
# e7 -fre-> e0). Without e2 the graph is consistent. GenMC's revisits leave
# this hole only once the prefix of e5 has an event of T0 past e2
# (GenMCDriver::isCoBeforeSavedPrefix).
e0: T0 W(x) rlx
e1: T0 F sc lkmm-fence:mb
e2: T0 W(y) rlx
e3: T0 R(y) rlx
e4: T1 TB acq
e5: T1 W(y) rlx
e6: T1 F sc lkmm-fence:mb
e7: T1 R(x) rlx
rf: e5->e3
mo(x): e0
mo(y): e2 e5
